# From Debug Log to Storytelling Gold: Turning Technical Insights into Compelling Narratives

---

## OPENING HOOK

*[Pause. Look at the audience.]*

Have you ever spent three days debugging a production issue? You finally find it. You fix it. You write up a post-mortem. And then… silence.

Your team reads it. Nods. And then… nothing changes.

Or worse—they forget. The same bug shows up six months later. A different team hits the same wall. The lesson dies in a document nobody reads.

*[Step forward.]*

Here's the uncomfortable truth: We're losing our best technical insights because we're telling them wrong.

We treat debugging lessons like incident reports. We say *what* happened. We list *who* did *what*. But we never explain *why it matters*.

